<p>Bed bugs may have stigma, but they hitchhike into all sorts of homes. Our bed bug work is for single-family, owner-occupied houses. We start with an inspection, because a few common things get mistaken for bed bugs, and what we find decides whether you need a treatment at all.</p>
<!-- details -->
<h2>How do you treat bed bugs?</h2>
<p>With residual treatments, including Aprehend, a fungus-based product that bed bugs pick up when they walk across treated areas. It's a cleanout with follow-up visits, and it won't wreck your bedroom furniture. Bed bug treatments also come with specific instructions for kids and pets, and we'll walk you through them.</p>

<h2>Is there a warranty?</h2>
<p>In a single-family, detached home, our bed bug treatments come with a 90-day warranty. The warranty doesn't cover apartments or one side of a duplex, where bed bugs can come right back from next door.</p>

<h2>Do you treat apartments?</h2>
<p>Generally, no. If you're a property manager who already works with us, text us. Otherwise, we'll point you toward someone else.</p>

<h2>Do you do heat treatments?</h2>
<p>No. When heat is the right answer, we'll tell you so and point you to someone we trust who does it.</p>

<h2>Should I do anything before the inspection?</h2>
<p>Not much. We'd rather you didn't do a ton of prep work before we've had a look. Once we know what we're dealing with, we'll tell you exactly what helps.</p>

<h2>What if you don't find any?</h2>
<p>Then we say so, and we don't sell you a treatment.</p>
